/ Stage 4 (ruling 8, decision 773): `set %x% = '{"a":1}' as json` lands %x% as
/ `{item, kind: json}` — json is item's, not text's, because a json value can hold any
/ value (number, bool, list, dict). Red today — the baseline is dict 5/5; %x!type.name%
/ reads "dict" (not "item"), so the first assert fails before the kind can be checked.
AsJsonKeepsJson
- set %x% = "{\"a\":1}" as json
- assert.equals(Expected="item", Actual=%x!type.name%, Message="type.name is item")
- assert.equals(Expected="json", Actual=%x!type.kind.name%, Message="type.kind.name is json")
